<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450335" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 1 — Index file title becomes root Ditamap title</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider an HTML package where the ZIP folder is named Printer_Docs. The index file contains</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>title</keyword>
        <keyword>HTML</keyword>
        <keyword>Printer</keyword>
        <keyword>Index</keyword>
        <keyword>User</keyword>
        <keyword>Guide</keyword>
        <indexterm>title</indexterm>
        <indexterm>HTML</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Printer</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
         <p>Consider an HTML package where the ZIP folder is named Printer_Docs. The index file contains a clear title, Printer User Guide, inside the <codeph>&lt;head&gt;</codeph> tag.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Title tag becomes ditamap title</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <p>ZIP folder name: <codeph>Printer_Docs</codeph></p>
                        <p>Index file: <codeph>index.html</codeph></p>
                        <p>Index file title: <codeph>&lt;head&gt;&lt;title&gt;Printer User Guide&lt;/title&gt;&lt;/head&gt;</codeph></p>
                        <p>HTML files: <codeph>installation.html</codeph>,
                              <codeph>maintenance.html</codeph></p>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_wsv_s45_lkc">
&lt;map>
    &lt;title>Printer User Guide&lt;/title>
    &lt;mapref href="installation.ditamap"/>
    &lt;mapref href="maintenance.ditamap"/>
&lt;/map></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> When an index file contains a valid HTML <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph> element, the converter uses that title (Printer User Guide) as the root Ditamap title. The ZIP folder name is used only when a suitable title is not present in the HTML package.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
